# ⚠ ORDER MATTERS IN THIS FILE: THE LAST MATCHING PATTERN WINS.
#
# The catch-all therefore comes FIRST and the dist/ exemptions come after it. A
# tidier-looking file with `* text=auto` at the bottom silently re-enables line
# ending translation for dist/ — the exact bug this file exists to prevent, and
# one that was written the wrong way round once already.

* text=auto

# ⚠ EVERYTHING IN dist/ IS BYTE-EXACT AND MUST NEVER BE TRANSLATED.
#
# The SDK verifies knv2lw.wasm and knv2lw.js against SHA-256 digests compiled
# into the bundle before it will let the engine instantiate, and
# checksums.sha256 publishes the digest of every shipped file.
#
# Git's autocrlf would rewrite the line endings of the text-looking files in
# dist/ on checkout — which changes their bytes, which changes their digests.
# The result for anyone cloning on Windows would be an IntegrityError on every
# chart, or a `shasum -c` that fails on a pristine clone, with nothing anywhere
# to explain why. Marking them binary is what makes the digests mean anything.
/dist/** -text -diff

# The digest list itself must stay LF, or `shasum -c` chokes on the line endings.
/checksums.sha256 text eol=lf
